+## Libre Terminal as a backend
+
+[Libre Terminal](https://github.com/samlazs/libre-terminal) is a local research
+terminal built on the OpenBB Platform. It answers the same `widgets.json`
+contract, so it can stand in for an openbq-docker stack on the same computer.
+
+Libre Terminal answers only its own page unless told otherwise. From release
+1.1, list this app's origins in `TERMINAL_EXTRA_ORIGINS` before starting it:
+
+- macOS and Linux: `export TERMINAL_EXTRA_ORIGINS="tauri://localhost http://tauri.localhost"`
+- Windows: `setx TERMINAL_EXTRA_ORIGINS "tauri://localhost http://tauri.localhost"`,
+  then open a new window.
+
+Then add two connections:
+
+- `http://127.0.0.1:6900` — the OpenBB widgets, financial statements included.
+- `http://127.0.0.1:6950` — Libre Terminal's own computed views. This one
+  serves no `apps.json`, so its card carries a note that apps could not be
+  read. That is expected.
+
+Use `127.0.0.1` or `localhost` exactly: Libre Terminal refuses any other host
+name, so it is reachable only from the computer it runs on. Without the
+setting, both connections show **Offline** with *Refused: this backend only
+answers the local terminal.*
+
+Statement view groups the lines of both its statement sources, Yahoo Finance
+and SEC. Widgets that open in a frame may show a refusal instead of their
+page: the frame's request carries no origin for Libre Terminal to match.
+
